{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/828643-help-with-npcs-portrayal","id":828643,"title":"Help with NPCs portrayal","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-02-12T00:16:13-08:00","id":828643,"title":"Help with NPCs portrayal","content":"Situation: a Silver Ladder Acanthus (fate 3 time 2 life 2) crossed path with a Gremlin Wizened serially punishing people for their &quot;sins&quot;, like using the Contracts of Artifice to make the car not work and have a car crash (to then die while going to the hospital). A Makara Beast (with Alien Allure) is also supporting him, by giving him potential victims (she leads a group of anti-violence center for women).<br /> <br /> Bastet, the Acanthus decided do go to the local freehold (about two hours distant from the city where the chronicle is located), and meet the Dawn King (a giant man with deer horns and powerful build, Striking Looks 2 and shirtless torso). After finding a way in thanks to a changeling friend, she's asking for justice, in<br /> The freehold has Dawn and Dusk Courts. What kind of reaction could the Dawn King have? What kind of support might he give to the mage player? Assuming I would prefer the cabal ultimately get the job down mostly on their own. <div align=\"center\"><img src=\"https://s-media-cache-ak0.pinimg.com/564x/49/60/52/4960525e1aa5511dc087b33f59b6b0a9.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/316-jesuncolo","name":"Jesuncolo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar316_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-12T12:51:09-08:00","id":828925,"title":"","content":"Well, Changelings tend to be a paranoid and secretive lot, so the Dawn King might ask for a pledge to make sure the Acanthus isn't telling others about the Freehold or bringing any more outsiders around. He might be perturbed with the Changeling who brought the Mage, too.<br /> <br /> If this Gremlin is a member of the Freehold, I'd think that they'd want to take care of the problem themselves, otherwise they might offer the usual kind of help with finding someone - known accomplices, hangouts, etc. (I think it would be unlikely that they'd disclose anything about the Hedge or Hollows, though.) They might even be willing to offer to send a Changeling NPC to help (and to make sure the Acanthus isn't up to anything shady). But, remember that the Dawn King will be wary of the Mage, would likely harbor some suspiciouns that the Mage is an agent of the Gentry, and would probably want something in return for any information or assistance, which could mean more pledges. The Mage would need to convince the monarch that they can be trusted.<br /> <br /> Or you could bring court politics into it. Maybe the Gremlin is a member of the Dusk court, and the Dawn King would like to see him taken out, but can't be connected to it. Of course, he'd want to make it out like he's still the one doing the Mage the favor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5910-csschulz","name":"CSSchulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5910_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}